    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207315658028_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Director of Enterprise Systems and Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nDelaware Valley University is seeking a collaborative and forward-thinking Director of Enterprise Systems and Services to provide strategic, technical, and operational leadership for the University’s enterprise application ecosystem. This role is responsible for ensuring the reliability, scalability, security, integration, and ongoing modernization of core administrative and academic systems, including the University’s Enterprise Resource Planning system and related enterprise platforms. The Director will serve as a key bridge between Technology Services and campus functional areas, helping translate institutional priorities into effective technology solutions that support student success and operational excellence. The Director of Enterprise Systems and Services will lead a team of technical professionals, guide enterprise system strategy, strengthen data integration and governance practices, and champion modern business processes across the institution. Key Responsibilities   Strategic and Operational Leadership Define the roadmap, architecture standards, and lifecycle management practices for the University’s ERP and related enterprise systems. Translate institutional priorities into clear operational plans, service-level expectations, and measurable technology outcomes. Establish standard operating procedures and strong change-management protocols. Promote modern software and integration practices that support system availability, performance monitoring, security, compliance, and data integrity. Team Leadership and Talent Development Lead, mentor, and empower a team of enterprise applications and integration professionals. Foster a proactive, accountable, service-oriented culture focused on continuous improvement and collaboration. Establish clear team objectives, encourage cross-training, and support ongoing professional development in emerging enterprise technologies. Systems Integration, Data, and Process Modernization Oversee data integration across platforms using modern APIs, batch pipelines, and integration middleware. Partner with functional leaders in areas such as Registrar, Financial Aid, Finance, Human Resources, Admissions, and others to evaluate and improve cross-departmental business workflows. Support institutional data governance, reporting, and operational data stores to enable reliable, data-informed decision-making. Serve as the senior technical escalation point for critical enterprise incidents, ensuring root-cause analysis, documentation, and clear stakeholder communication. Project Portfolio and Vendor Management Oversee the enterprise systems project portfolio using structured project management methodologies to ensure projects are delivered on time and within scope. Manage strategic relationships with enterprise software vendors, consultants, and service providers. Lead product evaluations, contract reviews, and resource planning to maximize the value of institutional technology investments. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field. At least five years of progressively responsible experience in enterprise systems architecture, administration, or integration. Equivalent combinations of education, professional certifications, and hands-on experience will be considered. Demonstrated success leading, mentoring, and developing technical personnel or cross-functional project teams. Strong understanding of enterprise architectures, relational databases such as MSSQL, and modern system integration methods, including REST/SOAP APIs, middleware, and ETL/ELT. Proven ability to execute and deliver complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise projects, implementations, or upgrades from initiation through adoption. Exceptional communication skills, including the ability to explain complex technical concepts to non-technical academic and administrative partners. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Information Systems, Technology Management, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience in higher education IT environments. Familiarity with student information systems and higher education ERP platforms, such as Ellucian Colleague. Hands-on experience with higher education integration and reporting platforms such as Ellucian Ethos, Informer, TransAct, operational data stores, or enterprise payment and commerce platforms such as TouchNet. Working knowledge of data governance frameworks and agile or ITIL service management principles. Work Environment This position operates in a standard office environment with options for flexible or hybrid scheduling. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required during critical institutional milestones, including peak registration periods, fiscal year-end close, scheduled maintenance windows, or major system cutovers. About the Role This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced enterprise systems leader who enjoys working at the intersection of technology, operations, data, and service. The successful candidate will be a strategic partner to campus stakeholders and a hands-on leader who can guide modernization, strengthen system reliability, and help advance the University’s mission through effective technology solutions. About the Company Delaware Valley University (DelVal) is a private, comprehensive, nonprofit university educating students with a curriculum that emphasizes and requires experiential learning. Located in Doylestown, Pennsylvania, about 30 miles north of Philadelphia, the University offers 28 undergraduate majors in business, arts and sciences, and agricultural and environmental sciences; 12 master's degrees; and a doctorate in education. Founded in 1896, DelVal has been cited by the National Society for Experiential Education as having the country's top experiential learning program, by Princeton Review as one of the best colleges in the Northeast, and by College Factual as having one of the top 20 animal science programs in the country. Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207171749152_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Men’s Lacrosse Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nJob Summary: This 9-Month, part time position will assist the head coach in all operations of the men’s lacrosse program including, but not limited to: practice planning and game preparation; coaching and scouting; recruitment of student-athletes; player development and support; academic monitoring; campus and community engagement efforts; fundraising and alumni development; scheduling; travel planning; budget management; and coaching personnel management. The ideal candidate will have defensive/goals experience.  All coaches are expected to advance the mission of the department of athletics to provide an environment that supports the academic and personal achievement of student-athletes. Coaches at Delaware Valley serve as educators and mentors who promote athletic achievement, personal growth and development of skills for life through the experiential learning of sport.  Coaches are expected to work cooperatively within the athletic department, the student affairs division, and across the entire Delaware Valley community to realize goals in support of student success and university goals and mission.  Primary Responsibilities:  Demonstrate effective coaching through content knowledge, practice construction and execution  Recruit prospective student athletes in accordance with the NCAA, MAC, and Delaware Valley University rules Instruct student athletes in physical health (strength & conditioning), individual/team concepts and safety. Provide general advising, mentoring, and support to student athletes Ensure and communicate expectations for student-athletes’ academic, conduct and other performance and engagement issues, collaborating appropriately with university personnel Help coordinate team travel, itineraries, housing and meals in a timely fashion in accordance with departmental policies and guidelines Collaborate with athletic training personnel regarding medical clearances, injury prevention, rehabilitation and playing status of student-athletes Promote and manage the development and coordination of university and community engagement and service activities that promote positive interaction between student-athletes and non-student athletes and community members Assess academic performance of student athletes to ensure ongoing eligibility  Other duties and responsibilities as assigned    The above job responsibilities are intended only to describe the general nature of the job and should not be construed as an all-inclusive list of position responsibilities.   Working Conditions and Frequently Used Tools:  Non-traditional hours Travel and driving for competition and recruiting Additional obligations assisting with university events (including but not limited to: admission and recruitment events; student welcome and orientation; alumni/advancement)    Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:  Demonstrate ability to recruit, inspire, mentor, coach and teach Demonstrated commitment to philosophy of Division III athletics program Evidence of commitment to academic and personal development of student-athletes Demonstrated experience and familiarity with recruitment of qualified students Strong managerial, administrative, organizational, and computer skills Excellent communication skills and demonstrated collegiality with colleagues within and beyond athletics Working knowledge of NCAA rules, regulations and related compliance issues. Must pass annual NCAA rules test Demonstration of leadership, sportsmanship and conduct becoming the coaching profession    Functional and Supervisory Relationships:  Works closely with the head coach, along with support staff to ensure success of DelVal Lacrosse   Required Education, Experience, and License:   Bachelor’s degree preferred  Prior successful experience coaching Experience coaching Defense, or Faceoffs preferred  CPR-First Aid/AED Certification Valid driver’s license required    Delaware Valley University (DelVal) is a private, comprehensive, nonprofit university educating students with a curriculum that emphasizes and requires experiential learning. Located in Doylestown, Pennsylvania, about 30 miles north of Philadelphia, the University offers 28 undergraduate majors in business, arts and sciences, and agricultural and environmental sciences; 12 master's degrees; and a doctorate in education. Founded in 1896, DelVal has been cited by the National Society for Experiential Education as having the country's top experiential learning program, by Princeton Review as one of the best colleges in the Northeast, and by College Factual as having one of the top 20 animal science programs in the country. Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
