      "title": "Student Worker - Dairy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nJob Summary: DVU Dairy is looking for a team of motivated individuals that have a genuine desire to learn through hands on work in the dairy facility. It is our desire to build a team of positive employees that are willing to learn and accomplish the many tasks that are required on a daily basis. Employees work an average of 15-20 hours per week, and one weekend per month. The schedule is reasonably flexible allowing students to take classes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities:  Mix and distribute feed to the different animal groups housed at the facility   Maintain a clean, healthy, and attractive facility   Clean and maintain bedded animal areas   Assist with the herd health care tasks  Maintain landscape areas such as mowing, trimming, and flower bed care  Assist with general maintenance of the facility  Other duties as assigned Education Employment eligibility: Currently enrolled Delaware Valley University student Must be authorized to work in the United States and provide required documentation to verify identity and employment eligibility Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:  Some farm and animal experience preferred but not necessary Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Occasionally lifting 25 lbs or less Frequently lifting 25 lbs or more Typically standing or walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Climbing ladders, scaffolds Using tools requiring high dexterity Outdoor exposure to weather Exposure to moving machinery Exposure to unpleasant odors Exposure to animal feces and specimens May be exposed to animal contagious diseases High noise environment High dust, dirt, grease environment May have an alternative work schedule May be required to be on-call Need to be able to be up early in the morning",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9206936559741_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Horticulture Production",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nJob Summary: Students will help assist in the maintenance of fruit trees and vegetable plants to produce fruits and vegetables for the Bucks County Opportunity Council, CHOP, and to be sold at the farm market on campus, Terrain, and the dining hall. Support academic labs and volunteer events involving the fruit and vegetable fields. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Operate farm equipment & tools used in all aspects of fruit and vegetable production, field management, and facility upkeep.   Scout fields to identify pests & issues that could affect quality or yield   Perform routine maintenance & upkeep of tractors & farm equipment and assist with field repairs as needed.  Complete tasks as specifically assigned  Communicate clearly & professionally at work, with other students & staff, and with supervisor  Recognize & immediate report broken or malfunctioning equipment  Occasionally assist other Ag Departments in emergence or for special projects  Other duties as assigned Education Employment eligibility: Currently enrolled Delaware Valley University student Must be authorized to work in the United States and provide required documentation to verify identity and employment eligibility Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Ability to lift bulky or awkward items (usually 20 lbs or more). Acceptable hand/eye/finger/leg/foot coordination needed to operate conventional farm equipment mechanism Valid driver’s license Horticulture production is primarily an outdoor operation in all types of weather, but also includes working inside the Ag Machinery shop, the horticulture building basement, and the greenhouses.  Proper attire can be influenced by weather, and students must always dress accordingly. Long pants and sturdy work boots are strongly emphasized at all times. Safety glasses, gloves, & ear protection are provided as needed, and students are fully expected to comply with DVU safety rules. Student workers should expect & come prepared for typical farm conditions including but not limited to: noise, dust, heat, cold, sun, darkness, dirt, oily/greasy, damp/wet, dry, and physically demanding situations.  Typically standing or walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Climbing ladders, scaffolds Typically running, climbing Exposure to chemicals Exposure to moving machinery Exposure to unpleasant odors Exposure to animal feces and specimens May be exposed to animal bites, scratches and contagious diseases",
      "department": ""
    },
