      "title": "Adjunct Pool, Department of Equine Science and Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2023-06-28\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nThe Equine Department seeks part-time temporary adjunct instructors for Equine Courses including Riding Skills Classes.   Ideal candidates should possess a Master’s degree and have experience teaching at the college level. Applying for a part-time teaching position would add the applicant to a pool to be considered in case another need arises in the future. To apply complete an application and submit a curriculum vitae to the online application. Additional documents may be required by the department at a later time.     Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances could include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania Patch, FBI Fingerprints completed by IDENTGO, and the Child Abuse History clearance.     Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200043811529_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Summer Youth Programs Team Member",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-03-30\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nSummer Youth Programs Team Member    Delaware Valley University (DelVal) is an academic leader in experiential learning, offering a combination of hands-on training and personalized academic attention since 1896. Located in Doylestown, Pennsylvania, DelVal offers 28 undergraduate majors, graduate degrees, continuing education, online career development, and certificate programs. The university is known for its 1,000-acre campus and distinctive programs in agribusiness, food science, animal science, and zoo science. With a 13:1 student-faculty ratio, DelVal provides hands-on learning through small class sizes across all disciplines. We are seeking energetic, experienced individuals to support our youth programs during the 2026 summer camp season. Youth Programs Team Members will assist instructors in specialty areas including Animal Science, Sports and Recreation, Theatre, Technology, Robotics, STEM, Digital Media, Arts, Coding, Literature, App and Game Design, and more! Flexible commitment: work for one to eight weeks depending on your availability. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assisting Instructional Specialists with classroom instruction during one-week programs Supporting youth participant supervision, engagement, care and daily needs Managing classroom dynamics and behavior Facilitating campus navigation, lunch, and health concerns Serving as a positive ambassador for the program Qualifications 18 years of age or older 2+ years of experience in youth leadership, programs, or direct work with children/teens Background in education, coaching, camp, childcare, social work, or psychology strongly preferred Strong communication skills with youth, peers, and families Collaborative team player with strong initiative Dependable, adaptable, and committed to creating a safe, inclusive environment Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances will include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check, the Pennsylvania Child Abuse History Certification, and the FBI Criminal Background Check completed by IDENTGO. Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200040324045_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Instructional Specialist Youth Programs",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-03-30\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nInstructional Specialist Youth Programs Delaware Valley University (DelVal) is an academic leader in experiential learning, offering a combination of hands-on training and personalized academic attention since 1896. Located in Doylestown, Pennsylvania, DelVal offers 28 undergraduate majors, graduate degrees, continuing education, online career development, and certificate programs. The university is known for its 1,000-acre campus and distinctive programs in agribusiness, food science, animal science, and zoo science. With a 13:1 student-faculty ratio, DelVal provides hands-on learning through small class sizes across all disciplines. We are seeking experienced K-12 and higher education instructors to teach summer specialty camps during the 2026 summer camp season and school-year programs during the 2026-2027 academic year. Instructional Specialists will lead one-week programs in areas including Equine Science, Animal Science, Theatre, Robotics, STEM, Digital Media, Arts, Coding, App and Game Design, and more. Flexible scheduling: work for one to eight weeks based on your availability. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Developing curriculum and creating engaging activities for K-12 participants  Delivering instruction in your area of specialization  Setting up and maintaining program areas  Supervising program participants and Youth Programs Team Members  Managing program inventory and materials  Creating a dynamic, hands-on learning environment Qualifications 18 years of age or older 4+ years of experience teaching or instructing K-12 or higher education students Extensive knowledge and experience in area of specialization Proven curriculum development and instructional design skills Experience supervising staff preferred Strong communication and classroom management abilities Collaborative team player with strong initiative Dependable, adaptable, and committed to creating a safe, inclusive environment Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances will include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check, the Pennsylvania Child Abuse History Certification, and the FBI Criminal Background Check completed by IDENTGO. Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200369778082_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool Ed.D Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-03-17\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nDelaware Valley University is currently searching for part-time adjunct faculty to instruct Ed.D. students in the Ed.D specialization areas of: Higher Education Administration, K-12 Program Design, Curriculum and Instruction, Instructional Technology, or School Operations . Accepting applications for graduate level courses.   Primary Responsibilities:   Teach a broad offering of concepts in the Ed.D specializations listed above Teach at various levels within the discipline   Effectively incorporate on-line learning options Provide data to support program and course Learning outcomes mastery  Post and maintain regular office hours    Other duties and responsibilities as assigned     Working Conditions and Frequently Used Tools:    Office, library, computer room  Typically sitting at a desk or table  Typically standing or walking  Occasionally lifting 25 lbs. or less  Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:     Evidence of successful scholarship  Excellent oral and written communication skills  Commitment to graduate teaching and mentoring Required Education, Experience, and License:    Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Higher Ed Administration, K-12 Administration, Ed Leadership, Curriculum and Instruction or related disciplines  Master’s degree in K-12 Administration/Educational Leadership, K-12 program design, evaluation and assessment, or related area  Specialization in K-12 Administration/Educational Leadership, K-12 program design, evaluation, assessment, or related disciplines  Experience teaching courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in K-12 Administration/Educational Leadership, K-12 program design and assessment or related disciplines Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances could include but are not limited to the Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check. Additionally, upon an acceptance of an offer of employment this position will require an official transcript verification.  Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and proud of our commitment to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200129779508_1&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Adjunct Digital Photography Instructor,  Media & Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2021-10-06\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nThe English department at Delaware Valley University seeks adjunct faculty members to teach Digital Photography classes.  Applications will be reviewed for fall and spring course work on a rolling basis.   Coursework that needs instructors include: •    Digital Photography I •    Digital Photography II Duties and Responsibilities:  Teach introductory Digital Photography course on an as needed basis. Hold one office hour per week per class.  This course will introduce the processes, principles, and tools of photography. Instruction will center around building a strong technical foundation in digital photography using DSLR cameras and/or Smartphones as well as digital editing and workflow using the Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop & Lightroom. Students will develop visual literacy regarding image creation and editing throughout a semester of looking at work, discussion, and critique. Students will walk away from this course with a portfolio of work and a solid foundation in photography. Minimum Requirements:  •      MFA Degree •      Must be fluent in Lightroom and Photoshop •      Must have some studio lighting experience Delaware Valley University reserves the right to revise, change or modify job responsibilities and position qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances could include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania Patch, FBI Fingerprints completed by IDENTGO, and the Child Abuse History clearance. Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
