      "title": "Adjunct Pool for Business Administration Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2020-07-26\n\nThe Department of Business and Information Management at Delaware Valley University is seeking adjunct faculty to teach Introduction to Business, Principles of Accounting, and Federal Income Tax at its Doylestown campus. Candidates must possess an MBA or Master's Degree; Doctorate is preferred. Those without a doctorate must have industry experience. Candidates with out-of-field degrees must have earned at least 15 graduate credits in the area of teaching assignment.      All applicants applying to this position with become part of the adjunct pool which is reviewed on a rolling basis.      Delaware Valley University reserves the right to revise, change or modify job responsibilities and position qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment.       Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances could include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania Patch, FBI Fingerprints completed by IDENTGO, and the Child Abuse History clearance.     Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and proud of our commitment to a diverse workforce.",
