    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=997c6fde-f713-4be9-b6cf-f4bdbc02cbbb&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=2576489235_3141&lang=en_US.html": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool- Graduate Level Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2018-08-16\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nThe Graduate Program of Arts in Criminal Justice program at Delaware Valley  University invites applications for adjunct instructor positions. This is a pooled position which will serve as an electronic file from which candidates will be drawn on an as needed basis. The program offers a hybrid model of instruction, wherein each class is 50% face-to-face and 50% online. Courses are offered in the evenings.   Complete applications are to include:    a cover letter  C.V.   Contact information for three professional references     Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis.     Future courses available for adjunct staffing may include:     Security Threat Groups  Advanced Criminology  Criminal Law and Procedure  Diversity and Criminal Justice Social Policy  Problems in Contemporary Corrections, Probation, and Parole  Ethical Leadership and Accountability in the Criminal Justice System    Preferred Requirements:    Ph.D.  in Criminal Justice, Public Safety, Criminology or Legal Studies   Demonstrated  teaching excellence   Experience  working with diverse populations     Minimum Requirements:     Master’s  degree with significant work experience in law enforcement administration,  public safety, courts, corrections, or homeland security.    Demonstrated  teaching excellence   Experience  working with diverse populations     Duties and Responsibilities:     Teach a specified course  Prepare course materials  Stay current on topics and practices related to the discipline  Provide support and guidance to students  Evaluate student performance  Participate in Outcomes Assessment practices  Work with Graduate Program Director  Learn and/or update the use of Blackboard (DE101 certification training provided)       Delaware Valley University reserves the right to revise, change or modify job responsibilities and position qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment.   Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances, appropriate to the position, that have been completed within the last 5 years. These clearances could include but are not limited to: Pennsylvania Patch, FBI Fingerprints completed by IDENTGO, and the Child Abuse History clearance.   Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and proud of our commitment to a diverse workforce.",
