      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Doylestown\n\nJob Summary: Clean and maintain University assets per the standard set forth by the Manager of Custodial Operations. This position is full-time, 12-months, reporting to the Manager of Custodial Operations.   There are three full-time openings available as follows:  1.  Saturday through Wednesday, First Shift – the hours are from 6 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. 2.  Wednesday through Sunday, Second Shift – the hours are from 2 p.m. to 10:30 p.m. 3.  Monday through Friday, Third Shift – the hours are from 10 p.m. to 6:30 a.m. Pay Rate : $18.50 per hour  (plus $.75 cents shift differential for second shift and $1.00 shift differential for third shift) Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Disposal of trash  Maintain cleanliness of assigned areas  Sweep, mop, and buff floors  Maintain aesthetic appearance of entrance to building  Make sure custodial closet is fully stocked and organized  Strip and wax floors as needed  Report facility issues to Facility Maintenance Office  Prep resident halls for each semester  Other duties and responsibilities as assigned Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions  Ability to interact with customers (students, faculty, administration), co-workers and supervisors in a positive and helpful manner Demonstrated aptitude for successful completion of assigned tasks  English proficiency is required Education and Experience: High School Diploma with 1 year direct and 2 years indirect experience  Prior floor care experience Physical Requirements and Working Conditions:  Valid state driver’s license  Must be in sound physical condition  Stockroom or warehouse  High noise environment  High dust, dirt, and grease environment  Requires extensive safety training  Exposure to moving machinery  Alternative work schedule may be required Exposure to chemicals  Requires protective devices  Occasional lifting 25-50 lbs.  Typically standing or walking  Typically bending, crouching, stooping   Special Message to Applicants :   Selected applicants will be responsible for providing the University with clearances appropriate to the position. These clearances include the Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check. Additionally, upon an acceptance of an offer of employment, this position will require a Motor Vehicle Report and a Physical Lift Examination.  All employment is provisional for 90 days.   During this 90-day period, custodians are not eligible for benefits and cannot join the Teamsters Union.  Delaware Valley University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to a diverse workforce.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
